facts:
  - "Gmail lists 25MB and Outlook.com lists 20MB. Whichever you use, the recipient's limit applies too, so the lower number is the one that counts."
  - "Attaching a file makes it about a third bigger, because email can only carry text and has to re-encode it. A 20MB video travels as roughly 27MB, which is why files near the limit bounce. Around 15MB is a safe target for any provider."
  - "Work accounts are stricter again. Exchange often defaults to 10MB, and IT can set it lower."
